  "consequences": [
    "Every tmQM run with n_train <= 1023 trained on a cohort with ZERO Pt (the old window is the first 5*n candidates and the first Pt sits at index 5118). n_train <= 176 is 100% Re. 13 of the 14 dataset:tmqm configs inherit DEFAULT_TRAIN_CLOUDS=256, which lands inside both regions.",
    "Any A/B between a small-n arm and cfm_tmqm_all6 (26715) conflates cohort size with metal diversity.",
    "The M2 measurement 'swapping the metal's atomic number moved the velocity by 0.74%' was taken on a checkpoint that may never have seen more than one metal, so it cannot be read as 'the metal channel is weak'."
  ],
  "honest_limits": [
    "The old mix is simulated, not re-loaded: the simulation reproduces the loader's own rng call sequence (randrange(n_seen) per candidate) over the filtered stream, and the build step skips 0 complexes on this corpus (measured: 'skipped 0 + 0'), so the simulation is exact for the metal counts.",
    "The new draw's mix is the quota applied to the real pool; the loader can still come up short if a drawn complex fails to build, and it prints a WARNING naming the metal and the shortfall when that happens.",
    "Every archived tmQM number was produced on a metal-biased cohort. None of them is comparable to a run on the fixed draw."
  ]
